            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1SA.24.1+1SA.24.2+1SA.24.3+1SA.24.4+1SA.24.5+1SA.24.6+1SA.24.7+1SA.24.8+1SA.24.9+1SA.24.10+1SA.24.11+1SA.24.12+1SA.24.13+1SA.24.14+1SA.24.15+1SA.24.16+1SA.24.17+1SA.24.18+1SA.24.19+1SA.24.20+1SA.24.21+1SA.24.22"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Sam 24.1-22",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Then the Ziphites came to Saul at Gibe-ah, saying, “Is not David hiding himself on the hill of Hachilah, which is on the east of Jeshimon?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So Saul arose and went down to the wilderness of Ziph, with three thousand chosen men of Israel, to seek David in the wilderness of Ziph. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Saul encamped on the hill of Hachilah, which is beside the road on the east of Jeshimon. But David remained in the wilderness; and when he saw that Saul came after him into the wilderness, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "David sent out spies, and learned of a certainty that Saul had come. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then David rose and came to the place where Saul had encamped; and David saw the place where Saul lay, with Abner the son of Ner, the commander of his army; Saul was lying within the encampment, while the army was encamped around him.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then David said to Ahimelech the Hittite, and to Joab's brother Abishai the son of Zeruiah, “Who will go down with me into the camp to Saul?” And Abishai said, “I will go down with you.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So David and Abishai went to the army by night; and there lay Saul sleeping within the encampment, with his spear stuck in the ground at his head; and Abner and the army lay around him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then said Abishai to David, “God has given your enemy into your hand this day; now therefore let me pin him to the earth with one stroke of the spear, and I will not strike him twice.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But David said to Abishai, “Do not destroy him; for who can put forth his hand against the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "'s anointed, and be guiltless?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And David said, “As the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " lives, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " will smite him; or his day shall come to die; or he shall go down into battle and perish. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " forbid that I should put forth my hand against the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "'s anointed; but take now the spear that is at his head, and the jar of water, and let us go.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So David took the spear and the jar of water from Saul's head; and they went away. No man saw it, or knew it, nor did any awake; for they were all asleep, because a deep sleep from the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had fallen upon them.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then David went over to the other side, and stood afar off on the top of the mountain, with a great space between them; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and David called to the army, and to Abner the son of Ner, saying, “Will you not answer, Abner?” Then Abner answered, “Who are you that calls to the king?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And David said to Abner, “Are you not a man? Who is like you in Israel? Why then have you not kept watch over your lord the king? For one of the people came in to destroy the king your lord. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "This thing that you have done is not good. As the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " lives, you deserve to die, because you have not kept watch over your lord, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "'s anointed. And now see where the king's spear is, and the jar of water that was at his head.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Saul recognized David's voice, and said, “Is this your voice, my son David?” And David said, “It is my voice, my lord, O king.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said, “Why does my lord pursue after his servant? For what have I done? What guilt is on my hands? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now therefore let my lord the king hear the words of his servant. If it is the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " who has stirred you up against me, may he accept an offering; but if it is men, may they be cursed before the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", for they have driven me out this day that I should have no share in the heritage of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", saying, ‘Go, serve other gods.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now therefore, let not my blood fall to the earth away from the presence of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "; for the king of Israel has come out to seek my life,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26.20",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gk: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "a flea",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "(as in 24.14)",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " like one who hunts a partridge in the mountains.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.20"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Saul said, “I have done wrong; return, my son David, for I will no more do you harm, because my life was precious in your eyes this day; behold, I have played the fool, and have erred exceedingly.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And David made answer, “Here is the spear, O king! Let one of the young men come over and fetch it. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " rewards every man for his righteousness and his faithfulness; for the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " gave you into my hand today, and I would not put forth my hand against the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "'s anointed. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1SA.26.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1SA.26.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1SA 26:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
